Question:
According to the China electric power industry standard "Technical Code for Underground Excavation Construction of Hydraulic Structures" (DL/T5099-2011), which of the following are correct principles for setting the safety monitoring frequency of hydraulic underground works?
A. Monitoring should be appropriately intensified within a range of 1.5 times the tunnel diameter from the excavation face;
B. After the surrounding rock becomes basically stable, the monitoring frequency may be gradually reduced;
C. When the deformation rate increases significantly, monitoring should be increased to at least once per day;
D. After the initial support is completed, monitoring shall still continue according to the plan;
E. The first monitoring shall be completed within 24 hours after excavation blasting.

In urban hydrological surveys, the main contents of the underlying surface condition survey usually include? ()
A. Urban land use conditions, such as built-up areas, undeveloped wasteland, park green space, water bodies, and low-lying areas;
B. Vegetation cover, soil type and properties, hydrogeological characteristics, etc.;
C. Urban nighttime light intensity index;
D. Total catchment area, permeable surface area, impermeable surface area, etc.

Regarding the comparison of characteristics between unconfined groundwater and confined groundwater, which of the following statements are correct?
A. Unconfined groundwater has a free water surface;
B. The recharge area and discharge area of confined groundwater are spatially consistent;
C. The circulation speed of confined groundwater is generally faster than that of unconfined groundwater;
D. Unconfined groundwater can directly receive recharge from atmospheric precipitation;
E. The discharge mode of confined groundwater is only spring emergence.

When a groundwater divide exists between a river and a canal, regarding the characteristics of its location, which of the following statements are correct?
A. The divide must be located exactly midway between the two rivers/canals;
B. The location of the divide is affected by the water-level difference between the two sides;
C. The divide is usually biased toward the river/canal with the higher water level;
D. If the water levels on both sides are the same, the divide is located in the middle.

A certain underground powerhouse has a maximum span of 25 m. According to the relevant code, what should be the minimum thickness of the overburden above the crown?
A. 25 m;
B. 50 m;
C. 5 m;
D. 12.5 m;
E. 30 m

In winter concrete construction, which of the following statements regarding preheating of raw materials is correct?
A. The heating temperature of mixing water should not exceed 60℃;
B. The maximum preheating temperature of coarse aggregate may be set to 70℃;
C. Cement needs to be stored in advance for 48h in a place not lower than 5℃;
D. Steam may be used directly to heat sand;
E. The mixing time should be reduced to 0.7 times the normal-temperature mixing time.

In the hydraulic design of a metal spiral casing, what is the key step that must be completed first?
A. Determine the connection structure between the spiral casing and the stay ring;
B. Select the wrap angle φ₀ and the average velocity v̄₀ at the inlet section;
C. Calculate the hydraulic coefficient C of the spiral casing;
D. Draw the plan single-line diagram of the spiral casing;
E. Determine the specific dimensions of the butterfly edge of the stay ring.

Regarding the functions and design requirements of a regulating pond, which of the following options are correct?
A. Priority should be given to arranging it on a fill foundation with poor geological conditions;
B. It can reduce the design flow of the downstream canal;
C. It usually needs to be taken out of service during the flood season to prevent siltation;
D. The downstream canal of the regulating pond should be designed for the minimum flow;
E. Whether it is set up should be determined through technical and economic comparison.

When a certain turbine runner is repaired by spray welding, which of the following operation steps are correct?
A. Directly spray-weld the runner at room temperature;
B. Use an oxy-acetylene flame to melt the alloy powder and spray it onto the surface;
C. Carry out static balance testing immediately after spray welding;
D. Preheat the runner before welding
E. Grind the surface of the weld layer after spray welding

Regarding the structural characteristics of the water diversion chamber of a reaction hydraulic turbine, which of the following options are correct?
A. An open water diversion chamber is suitable for Francis turbines with heads exceeding 120 m;
B. A tank-type water diversion chamber is usually used only for small turbines because the flow must turn sharply;
C. When a metal spiral case adopts a circular cross-section, the steel plate thickness of its inlet section needs to be adjusted according to the stress conditions;
D. The wrap angle of a concrete spiral case is mostly designed as 180°~270°;
E. A tubular turbine must adopt a spiral-case-type water diversion chamber structure.

During the construction of a roller-compacted concrete dam in China, the main inspection indicators used to evaluate the quality of interlayer bonding should include:
A. interlayer shear strength;
B. permeability coefficient;
C. VC value loss rate;
D. aggregate segregation degree;
E. temperature rise value

In China, which of the following are usually included in the specific work content of quality control during the construction stage of a project?
A. Reviewing the technical rationality of construction drawings;
B. Tracking and inspecting the acceptance process of concealed works;
C. Sampling and inspecting the testing instruments and equipment used by the contractor;
D. Preparing the project feasibility study report;
E. Participating in the reporting and handling of major quality accidents.

Which of the following methods help control the hydration heat temperature rise of mass concrete?
A. Use low-heat cement;
B. Pre-cool the coarse aggregate;
C. Add 30% fly ash;
D. Increase the pouring layer thickness to 5 m;
E. Use ice mixing to reduce the concrete discharge temperature.

Regarding shaft pilot-hole construction, in Class I and II surrounding rock, which of the following statements are correct?
A. The cross-sectional area of the pilot hole is usually designed as 4-5㎡;
B. When using the bottom-up excavation method, a through pilot hole must be drilled first;
C. The raise climber method is suitable for deep shaft construction;
D. The raise boring machine method is especially suitable for soft rock strata;
E. The shaft enlargement process must strictly follow the top-down sequence.

A construction contract for a certain project stipulates that liquidated damages for delay are calculated at 0.1% of the contract price per day, and the total contract price is 100 million yuan. Please determine how many of the following statements are correct?
① A 30-day delay requires compensation of 3 million yuan;
② The total amount of liquidated damages shall not exceed 10 million yuan;
③ Delays caused by force majeure (such as heavy rain) may be exempted from liability for compensation;
④ The employer has the right to directly deduct the liquidated damages from the progress payment;
⑤ The calculation base for liquidated damages includes provisional sums.

A. 2
B. 3
C. 4
D. 5

The total investment of a certain water conservancy project is 10 billion yuan. An audit finds that 30% of the funds were wasted. What is the amount of waste?
A. 3 billion yuan;
B. 0.3 billion yuan;
C. 1.5 billion yuan;
D. 6 billion yuan

A contractor wins a water conservancy and hydropower project contract with a contract price of 80 million yuan and is required to submit performance security according to the contract. If a guarantee letter is used, which of the following options may meet the required guarantee amount?
A. 4 million yuan;
B. 7.2 million yuan;
C. 9.6 million yuan;
D. 12 million yuan;
E. 16 million yuan.

The contract amount of a project is 120 million yuan, and performance security is submitted in the form of a bank guarantee. Which of the following options may be a reasonable guarantee amount?
A. 6 million yuan;
B. 9 million yuan;
C. 12 million yuan;
D. 15 million yuan;
E. 18 million yuan.

Regarding the relationship between the piezometric head line and the total head line, which of the following statements is incorrect? ()
① The total head line of a real fluid always decreases along the flow direction;
② The piezometric head line is lower than the total head line, and the difference is the velocity head;
③ Since the pressure head is the difference between the piezometric head and the elevation head, the piezometric head line must be above the elevation head line;
④ The piezometric head line may rise, fall, or remain unchanged.

A. ①②③④ are all incorrect
B. ②③ are incorrect
C. ③ is incorrect
D. ①④ are incorrect

Among the following descriptions of the main characteristics of non-uniform flow in open channels, which combination is correct?
① The water depth of the flow section and the section-averaged velocity vary along the flow path;
② Streamlines on the same flow section are approximately parallel straight lines;
③ The hydraulic gradient line, piezometric head line, and channel bed slope line are not parallel to each other;
④ The total mechanical energy (total head) gradually decreases along the flow path.
A. ①②④
B. ②③④
C. ①③④
D. ①②③④

Which of the following adverse effects of secondary circulation in bends is not included?
A. Reduced discharge capacity of sluice openings on the convex bank;
B. Intensified riverbed scour downstream of the concave bank;
C. A pronounced transverse water-surface slope forms in front of the sluice;
D. Increased sediment concentration at the intake.

Regarding fluid viscosity and its influencing factors, which of the following statements are correct?
A. The viscosity of water increases as temperature rises;
B. The viscosity of air decreases as temperature rises;
C. The viscosity of liquids is mainly controlled by intermolecular cohesive forces;
D. The viscosity of gases mainly depends on momentum exchange due to molecular thermal motion.

Regarding the vertical distribution law of suspended sediment concentration, which of the following statements are correct?
A. The larger the suspended index Z value, the more uneven the vertical distribution of sediment concentration;
B. If the sediment diffusion coefficient in the Rouse equation is equal to the momentum diffusion coefficient of the flow, the vertical distribution of sediment concentration is exponential;
C. When the suspended index Z = 5, sediment is almost not suspended;
D. When calculating the suspended index Z, it is more reasonable to use the shear velocity corresponding to sand-grain resistance;
E. In the derivation of the Rouse formula, the vertical turbulent diffusion coefficient is assumed to be constant.

In China, a certain three-phase asynchronous motor has 3 pole pairs and is connected to a 50 Hz power supply. Its synchronous speed should be which of the following?
A. 1000 r/min;
B. 1500 r/min;
C. 3000 r/min;
D. 600 r/min;
E. 750 r/min.

Regarding the equivalent models of practical power sources, which of the following descriptions are correct?
A. The internal resistance of an ideal voltage source is zero;
B. A practical current source can be represented as an ideal current source in parallel with an impedance;
C. The graphical symbol of an AC voltage source is the same as that of a DC voltage source;
D. Considering the external circuit, an ideal current source can provide infinite power;
E. The voltage-source model and current-source model of a practical power source can be equivalently converted into each other.

A current transformer has a ratio of 1000/5, and the secondary-side load is a 5 Ω resistor. If the primary current is 600 A, what is the approximate secondary-side output voltage?
A. 3 V;
B. 15 V;
C. 30 V;
D. 60 V;
E. 120 V.

For an ideal transformer, the turns ratio is 0.5. If the primary current is 5 A, the secondary current is:
A. 10 A;
B. 5 A;
C. 20 A;
D. 2.5 A;
E. 15 A.

In an RL circuit, the inductance L=2 H, the resistance R=4 Ω, and the initial steady-state current is 3 A. If the switch is suddenly opened, the time required for the inductor current to decay from 3 A to 1.1 A is approximately:
A. 0.25 s;
B. 0.5 s;
C. 1.0 s;
D. 1.5 s;
E. 2.0 s.

For a circuit with a time constant τ of 20 ms, approximately how long does it take for the transient process to basically end and the circuit to enter steady state?
A. 20 ms;
B. 40 ms;
C. 60 ms;
D. 100 ms;
E. 5 ms

Given that the characteristic equation of a voltage source is U=20-4I (V), when the output current is 2 A, its terminal voltage is:
A. 12 V;
B. 16 V;
C. 18 V;
D. 20 V;
E. 28 V

A non-salient-pole synchronous motor has the following operating parameters: line voltage U = 380 V, no-load electromotive force per phase E₀ = 250 V, and synchronous reactance Xc = 5.1 Ω. When the power angle θ = 30°, which of the following is the approximate electromagnetic power PM?
A. 16.1 kW;
B. 25.8 kW;
C. 31.6 kW;
D. 42.7 kW;
E. 50.3 kW.
